      {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "text": "## Lean\n\nAll other Lean is folded into one **Lean** line, because it matters to Lean, not to the reader. That includes imports (the folded line at the top), structures, quick checks such as `example`, and LaTeX notation rules. This one checks that doubling 3 gives 6, and tells the LaTeX view how to write `Basics.double`:",
        "line": 30
      },
      {
        "kind": "lean",
        "text": "example : Basics.double 3 = 6 := rfl\n\nopen Lean LeanTeX in\nlatex_pp_app_rules (const := Basics.double)\n  | _, #[n] => do\n    let n ← latexPP n\n    return LatexData.atomString \"\\\\operatorname{double}\" ++ n.parens",
        "line": 35,
        "items": [
          {
            "type": "code",
            "text": "example : Basics.double 3 = 6 := rfl\n\nopen Lean LeanTeX in\nlatex_pp_app_rules (const := Basics.double)\n  | _, #[n] => do\n    let n ← latexPP n\n    return LatexData.atomString \"\\\\operatorname{double}\" ++ n.parens"
          }
        ]
      },
